  "summary": "Telegram-controlled remote shell and filesystem exfiltration",
  "details": "The package installs a Telegram bot that binds inbound Telegram messages to shell execution on the host. Message handlers in core route `update.message.text` (and a `/com` command) into `subprocess.check_output(cmd, shell=True,..., timeout=120)`, giving any authorized Telegram sender arbitrary command execution on the machine running the bot. Additional handlers (`dumpall`, `getall`, `download`) read arbitrary files, package directories (default target `/`) into archives, and send them back over the Telegram Bot API, enabling full-filesystem exfiltration. The bot token and owner identifiers are supplied by the operator, but the package's core capability is a remote shell and file-exfil channel operated over a third-party messaging service.",
